10:40:02 | INFO | 🤖 Target: For **drop impacts**, yes: tough plastics such as polycarbonate are generally more durable than glass because they are far less likely to fracture. But “durable” is not limited to cracking. In engineering it includes resistance to wear, scratching, UV, chemicals, heat, and loss of optical performance. On those measures, glass often lasts longer. So the non-misleading statement is: > **Plastic is tougher and more drop-resistant; glass is harder and more wear-resistant.** Your common-sense conclusion is right for the failure mode you care about: a phone that survives being dropped. A scratched but functioning plastic-covered screen is often preferable to a pristine-looking glass screen that can crack catastrophically.
